in other people's virus.

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:14.133
Yeah, I'm just using that as example.

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.520
Yeah, but you can't breathe back in

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:19.260
so it's just breathing out but you never

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:22.560
take a breath back in, so
whenever you stop talking

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:26.830
you're holding your breath
again and that is not

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:29.110
absolutely normal.

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:29.943
Right.

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:32.540
Anyway.

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:34.400
But where I was going with that

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:37.530
was I haven't had an opportunity
to go outside very much

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:39.660
because it's been raining so much.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:42.070
I think this is our
last week of crazy rain

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.260
and then it's gonna get back

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.410
to more like Southern California.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:48.090
But there was a moment of sunshine.

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:50.150
It wasn't very warm,
I mean for California,

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:52.023
it was like 55 degress,
which we're still like,

00:12:52.023 --> 00:12:55.570
"Oh, that's a jacket."
It's like a blizzard to me.

00:12:55.570 --> 00:13:00.570
But because the sun
came out I went outside

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:06.050
and actually took my shirt
off, got down just to my pants

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:12.150
and took my meditation cushion out there

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:15.750
and started doin' some
yoga, I did some meditation,

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:19.560
I mean I just became an
amateur guru out there

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.973
on my basketball area out here.

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:25.463
Amateur guru is not a thing.

00:13:27.331 --> 00:13:29.223
Those words cancel each other out.

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:32.270
That's why I said amateur.
Wannabe guru, I think.

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:34.210
Wannabe guru.
Sure.

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.687
Nah, I don't think you're a wannabe guru.

00:13:36.687 --> 00:13:39.380
And I think at this point, just sidebar,

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:43.857
my air conditioner, heater came on.

00:13:43.857 --> 00:13:46.670
There's gonna be a lotta
noise in this podcast,

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:49.380
just get over it.
No one cares.

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:50.700
I'm not gonna apologize for it again.

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:51.913
Everybody was over it.

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:59.400
I was out there, first of all
I was just enjoying myself

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:03.840
just beyond words, and you know
I've gotten really flexible.

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:05.430
Have you seen how flexible I am now?

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:06.263
No.

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:10.230
I know I've been moving
around like a real old man

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:13.470
in all our vlogs, it's because of my knee,

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:15.650
but my knee is basically healed.

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:19.250
It took almost two months
for my knee to get healed.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.880
So I'm kinda back to my spry self now.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:22.713
Okay, yeah.

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:26.800
Just in time to do nothing.
Yeah, exactly.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.373
Just in time to stay at home.

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:31.770
But I was doing all kinds of,

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:35.100
I was going on the internet,
looking at moves, doin' em.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.800
But then I just started to
kinda walk around out there

00:14:38.889 --> 00:14:41.090
and just take in the sun,

00:14:41.090 --> 00:14:44.060
and then I realized that,
oh, I just walked up

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:47.340
to the window to the guest bedroom,

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:51.470
which is where Jessie is
currently on her ladies' chat.

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:52.343
Ah!

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:56.860
So what was, she hasn't told
me about this, by the way.

00:14:56.860 --> 00:14:59.320
She told Christy that

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:04.380
she saw someone walk by and she thought

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:08.620
it was a shirtless
vagrant, like her emotional

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:13.150
and knee-jerk reaction was fear.

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:15.780
Yeah.
She was deeply afraid

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:20.780
because her husband
walked past the window,

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:24.460
and then it took her a couple of beats

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:28.217
and then she was like,
"Wait, that was my husband."

00:15:29.696 --> 00:15:31.640
What have you done, man?

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:33.707
I mean, like--
Well, I will say--

00:15:33.707 --> 00:15:35.680
You're gallivantin' around your house

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:39.470
and you're puttin' your
own family in fear.

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:43.020
Well, the other day--
This means something.

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:45.670
The other day, I was walking
through the neighborhood,

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:47.683
just by myself--
Shirtless?

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:53.670
No, but I didn't look well-kept.

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:56.050
No, no you don't.
Right.

00:15:56.050 --> 00:16:00.253
And I had on a hoodie and
some un-matching sweatpants.

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:05.020
And like hiking shoes.
Okay.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:06.280
'Cause it was the day we thought

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:09.160
we were gonna go to the trail.

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:09.993
Yeah.

00:16:09.993 --> 00:16:13.640
And I know what my hair, listen.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:15.990
I've seen the comments,
I've seen all the people

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:19.060
requesting beard or hair trims.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.210
At this point it's
definitely not gonna happen.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:24.350
I feel like I've been preparing
for this moment all my life

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:26.490
to look like this during this pandemic.

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:28.560
You were ahead of the curve.

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:31.110
But I was walking through the neighborhood

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:32.750
and I started realizing that

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:40.600
it could easily be perceived
that a homeless man

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:44.230
has left some urban area and is now

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:49.120
up into the neighborhoods
looking for a place to bed down.

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:51.460
His territory has expanded.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:53.223
And I got a little paranoid.

00:16:55.281 --> 00:16:56.350
Oh, you got paranoid.

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:59.940
And then all of a sudden,
at the height of my paranoia

00:17:00.970 --> 00:17:02.778
I hear whoop whoop,

00:17:02.778 --> 00:17:04.880
you know, like when the cops
do that thing where they

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:06.460
make that little noise.
Oh, sure!

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:09.290
They chirp it up.
A cop chirped you?

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:14.290
I turn around and there's a
cop like flying towards me.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:16.087
What?
With his lights on

00:17:16.087 --> 00:17:19.360
and the siren, and he's
chirpin', he's whoop whoop,

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:21.200
woop-woop-woop-woop-woop-woop
bwoop-bwoop-bwoop,

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:24.023
almost like a record
scratch with the chirp.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.940
And I'm like, somebody has called and said

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.380
that there's a vagrant walking
through the neighborhood.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:30.657
It was probably your wife!

00:17:30.657 --> 00:17:33.777
And the cop is coming after me,

00:17:33.777 --> 00:17:35.813
but then he just goes right past me.

00:17:35.813 --> 00:17:37.640
You shoulda just got down.
He went right past me.

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:39.130
Put your hands behind
your head or somethin'.

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:41.330
But I was thinking about
what I was gonna say.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:43.410
I was like, "Nah, nah, I live here!"

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:45.530
And I was realizing that
no matter what I said

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:47.110
everything was gonna sound made up.

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:49.490
I haven't been cutting my
hair because of therapy.

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:50.813
It's a long story.

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:52.980
I was actually thinking about this today

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:56.773
that even if I made a decision to trim,

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:00.010
I'm not gonna cut my
own hair at this point.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:03.128
Yeah, well, you could,
I'm not saying you could.

00:18:03.128 --> 00:18:06.210
I'm not saying you couldn't,
I'm saying you should.

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:09.400
But just to check in on that,

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:10.973
I don't feel like I've,

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.973
I don't feel like I've
learned my lesson yet,

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:15.673
you know what I'm saying?

00:18:15.673 --> 00:18:17.163
You know if you listen to that Ear Biscuit

00:18:17.163 --> 00:18:19.103
there's a reason I'm growing it out.

00:18:19.103 --> 00:18:21.690
I don't think I've learned
what I need to learn yet.

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:23.193
I've learned that a lot of people,

00:18:24.054 --> 00:18:27.730
I've learned that it's polarizing,
that's what I've learned.

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:29.650
Well, I think also have learned to, like,

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:31.700
keep a shirt on whenever possible,

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:33.433
stay off the streets,

00:18:34.850 --> 00:18:36.850
try to get your sweatsuit to match

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.350
if you're going out in public,

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:42.720
just do a little somethin'
for yourself, you know?

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:45.870
I actually have some
thoughts about self-care

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:49.123
in this environment I'll
get to a little bit later.

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:54.810
For right now, let's plug the store.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:57.390
Okay.
Mythical.com, go there.

